  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own 'Five Years Financial Summary' multi-year summary table (audited), Solo/Standalone basis. Reporting basis confirmed by matching this dataset's recorded Total Assets against the bank's own separate (Solo) Balance Sheet, which is consistently lower than its Consolidated Balance Sheet (the bank consolidates an Offshore Banking Unit and a brokerage subsidiary, SJIBL Securities Limited) -- directly verified in FY2013, FY2014, FY2020, FY2022 and FY2025 (see sources.json). As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, Shahjalal Islami Bank PLC reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investment'/'Non-Performing Investment' rather than 'NPL', consistent with the convention used elsewhere in this dataset for EXIMBANK and FIRSTSBANK. Total Liabilities is not a separate line in the summary table and is calculated as Total Assets minus Total Shareholders' Equity. RESTATEMENT FOUND: Tier 2 Capital for FY2019 is contemporaneously reported as 12,770mn (Tier2 ratio 6.99%, Total Capital 29,277mn, Capital Surplus 11,000mn, CRAR 16.02%). The FY2020 annual report's comparative column restates this to 11,970mn (Tier2 ratio 6.55%, Total Capital 28,477mn, Capital Surplus 10,200mn, CRAR 15.58%) -- a genuine ~800mn reduction in recognised Tier 2 capital, stable in every subsequent report (2021-2025) that carries a FY2019 comparative. Tier 1 Capital, RWA, and all Financial Position / Operating Result rows are unaffected. Contemporaneous FY2019 figures (Tier2 12,770 / CRAR 16.02%) are kept per project rule. Separately, Total Deposits (203,384 own vs 203,273 per FY2020+ reports, -111mn/-0.05%) and Total Assets (266,104 own vs 265,993 per FY2020+ reports, -111mn/-0.04%) show a trivial, likely-rounding-level divergence, just at/under the 0.05% flag threshold; Non-Profit Earning Assets absorbs the entire 111mn difference (46,286 -> 46,175) while Profit Earning Assets is unchanged, consistent with a minor reclass rather than an economic restatement.",
